# Browser
# Spider-Sense's web-slinging {U}: "You may cast this spell for {U} if you also return a tapped creature you control to its
# owner's hand." The creature must be tapped when the costs are paid, not before casting began (CR 601.2g-h, 702.188a;
# ruling 2025-09-19): Bot1's only creature, Birds of Paradise, is untapped when Bot2 bolts Bot1, so web-slinging is offered
# because the Birds could tap for mana while it is paid. Bot1 web-slings Spider-Sense at the Bolt, taps the Birds for the
# {U}, and only then chooses the creature to return: the Birds, tapped for that very mana. The Forest, tapped too, is no
# creature. The Bolt is countered and Bot1 stays at 20, with the Birds back in hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Birds of Paradise
Spider-Sense
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Birds of Paradise.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Hand.Spider-Sense.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt; Ability: Web-slinging)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Birds of Paradise.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Birds of Paradise.Activate(Color: Blue)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Spider-Sense: choose a tapped creature to return to its owner's hand to pay for it
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Birds of Paradise)
? Stack = Spider-Sense; Lightning Bolt
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Birds of Paradise
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest
Bot1.Graveyard = Spider-Sense
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
